[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/multi_interface/pretense/multi_interface_impl_pretense.py: [slug:stream_writer.write.empty_payload] [viol:pret_qa.uncontracted_state_rule] Facet: empty payload write exception expectation Witness: sequence=write(payload=''), written_count=0, unread_count=0. The write override in MultiInterfacePseudoStateMachine forwards the drawn payload to the real StreamBuffer target without modeling the contracted operational postcondition for an empty payload: when the drawn payload is the empty string '' on a freshly seeded buffer (written_count=0, unread_count=0), low/stream_writer.pyi requires PayloadEmptyError to be raised and the buffer contents and written count to remain unchanged, yet the pseudo state machine currently lets that exception escape unhandled and aborts the run instead of observing the contracted empty-payload rejection; the write transition must expect the contracted PayloadEmptyError when len(payload) == 0 and continue with model state unchanged, covering the minimal counterexample sequence whose only operation after seeding is write(payload='').
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/multi_interface/pretense/multi_interface_impl_pretense.py: Resolved empty-payload feedback: the StreamBuffer write override now models the contracted empty-payload rejection by observing PayloadEmptyError via with raises(PayloadEmptyError) around the call_target pivot when len(payload) == 0, keeping buffer contents and written_count unchanged, then re-asserting SUT/model consistency; non-empty payloads continue through the normal write path.
